Reason:
These two __hci_cmd_sync() calls are made without holding hci_req_sync_lock, allowing a concurrent btintel_shutdown_combined() (which holds the lock) to free the response skb while btintel_hw_error() still accesses it, causing a slab-use-after-free.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
+	hci_req_sync_lock(hdev);
+		goto unlock;
+unlock:
+	hci_req_sync_unlock(hdev);
Reason:
Adding hci_req_sync_lock() at the start and hci_req_sync_unlock() after all operations serializes btintel_hw_error() with other synchronous HCI command issuers like btintel_shutdown_combined(). The goto unlock ensures that the lock is released on every exit path, preventing the race.

